BashKitten corresponding source and build material is published with each release:
https://github.com/openresearchtools/bashkitten

The browser derives from Mozilla Firefox ESR, Waterfox and WildBuzzard. Their
original licenses and attribution remain with the source. Exact retained donor
revisions are recorded in browser/bashkitten/upstreams.toml and ports.toml;
WildBuzzard's original source is https://github.com/openresearchtools/WildBuzzard.
The release metadata identifies the exact BashKitten and Firefox revisions.

The native command entry is browser/browser/app/BashKittenCommandLine.cpp;
commands execute in Gecko using its in-tree JsonCpp library. Tor, blocker assets
and other bundled components retain full licenses and corresponding build/source
material. Agent, Pi, search and authentication components carry their own notices.
The desktop package and paired Termux backend bundle private Node/npm and Pi
runtimes with their own full notices. Python, the Termux host application and
external operating-system libraries retain their separately installed package
licenses. Downloaded AI runtimes and models retain their original upstream
licenses; their source and download records are available under About > Licenses
> AI runtimes and models.
